      "content": "That makes sense, I'll definitely look into the hydrothermal vent possibility and check the sensor calibration. But there's one more thing—when I look at the timestamps for these erratic jumps, they aren't just random; they seem to happen in little bursts, almost like a glitch or some kind of persistent, annoying error that keeps popping up in the middle of otherwise perfect data sets. It's really frustrating to clean up. Does that sound like a known hardware issue or something else?",
